  - alias: Forge (agentic workspace)
type: software
version: v0.2.1
date-released: 2026-11-12
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/bdrazn/certified-L-eval
keywords:
  - elliptic curves
  - L-functions
  - BSD conjecture
  - interval arithmetic
  - ball arithmetic
  - Arb
  - certification
  - number theory
abstract: >-
  Machine-checked balls for L(1), L'(1) and L''(1) of elliptic curves over Q,
  built on a machine-verified pointwise involution law for the a_n stream and
  python-flint (Arb) ball arithmetic, with derived error budgets, selftest
  gates (Hecke + pointwise law + perturbation), and a cross-implementation
  harness against fresh PARI/GP lfun references validated at the 100- and
  500-digit rungs, extended in v0.2.0 with a detector-battery pipeline for full
  per-curve BSD audits (rank, parity, certified |Sha|-implied square test) with
  complete provenance, and in v0.2.1 validated further by a Tier-0 bridge: 100
  seeded random rank-2 curves audited end-to-end with 100/100 agreement and
  zero alarms.
